+ 
+ There&#x27;s almost entirely no sound at all. No music, no sfx. You just right click areas to do stuff, rather than feeling like you&#x27;re actually playing a game. There&#x27;s no quests, and no story. 
+ 
+ So far, I walk over to the iron, mine the iron, walk to town to sell, buy some stuff for my outpost, walk to outpost, wait for build, then walk back to iron, repeat. That loop takes like 15 minutes, and considering you just right click on the map to move, almost the ENTIRE 15 minutes is literally just me staring at the screen do it&#x27;s thing, with zero input. Realistically, this is almost an idler game. However, if you do in fact idle and go AFK, some random little thing will attack you, and since you don&#x27;t give inputs (or it&#x27;s too strong) you just lose. Losing &quot;can&quot; be as simple as being injured and needing to hobble back to town, or, as in my one case, you&#x27;re unconscious, with no food or medicine, so you can&#x27;t do anything at all to help yourself, and you just die. Gameover, because it&#x27;s permadeath. So you&#x27;re forced to sit there watching the painfully long walk, the extremely painfully long mining process, etc. I&#x27;m sure there&#x27;s good elements to this game, it looks super promising, but WOW it&#x27;s boring to actually sit through, and you MUST sit through it, or else keep making backup saves in case it goes bad.
+ 
+ I&#x27;m still really wanting to get into it, because I can see there&#x27;s a gem here, but it&#x27;s a diamond in the rough... a lot of rough... and I just don&#x27;t want to subject myself to painfully boring torturously bad gameplay, just for that little nugget of goodness.</div></div></details></div><div class="claim"><p class="text">Reviewers describe the game controls as janky, clunky, and poorly adapted for controllers.</p><details><summary><span class="tag mono">▸ 3 reviews</span><span class="cta">Show receipts</span></summary><div class="citation"><div class="meta mono">▼ does not recommend · 1.0 hrs · 2026-06-01</div><div class="body">I really did try to love Kenshi. I watched ambiguous amphibian&#x27;s playthroughs, watched a few hours worths of tips and tricks for noobs and none of it helped. Here&#x27;s a couple of gripes that I have only having played an hour(mainly cuz I wanted to give myself the choice of refunding).
