+
+ Well, I stand here now having installed the game and tried it for myself, and... &quot;underwhelmed&quot; doesn&#x27;t do it justice.  Have you ever played really old MMO&#x27;s, like EverQuest or DAOC?  Imagine hopping back in now, same graphics and all, and there was no tutorial or training missions to at least familiarize yourself with the controls.  Great, I did it to myself again, I purchased yet another game where I&#x27;m expected to watch hours of Youtube videos for stuff that the game itself refuses to teach.
+
+ There seems like there&#x27;s potential here, if you want a super sandboxy open world type thing where there isn&#x27;t any sort of story, plot, or world events.  It does seem to be one of those &quot;Everything and the kitchen sink, too&quot; sort of games, where if you have an idea - you can accomplish it.  I&#x27;m just typically not that creative, and need at least SOME degree of direction  to start playing a game. 
+
+ I may revise my review in the future if I give it another try, but I fear that this may be one of those games that&#x27;s going to be more interesting to watch other people play, than to actually play myself.  Maybe I&#x27;m missing something, but my brain was practically SCREAMING at me, &quot;Now what?&quot;.
