+
+ I may revise my review in the future if I give it another try, but I fear that this may be one of those games that&#x27;s going to be more interesting to watch other people play, than to actually play myself.  Maybe I&#x27;m missing something, but my brain was practically SCREAMING at me, &quot;Now what?&quot;.
+
+ **Update with more detail**
+ Gave it one more quick shot since I&#x27;m a bit of a masochist / hate wasting money on something I just purchased.  I genuinely feel like I&#x27;m missing something crucial to having fun here, because both times I got dropped into the &quot;Wanderer&quot; start - I felt like a toddler who was abandoned in the middle of an airport; confused, lost, directionless, and perhaps a bit scared.  After wandering aimlessly around the starting are…</div></div></details></div></div></section><section class="cohort"><h2>2-20h</h2><div class="stats mono">2-20 hours · 87.4% positive, based on 293 reviews</div><p class="summary">Players entering the world find themselves dropped into danger without guidance or hand-holding.</p><div class="theme"><h3>Difficulty</h3><div class="claim"><p class="text">Reviewers describe the opening hours as unguided and lacking a tutorial, dropping players into a dangerous world without direction.</p><details><summary><span class="tag mono">▸ 3 reviews</span><span class="cta">Show receipts</span></summary><div class="citation"><div class="meta mono">▲ recommends · 15.0 hrs · 2026-07-22</div><div class="body">As far as RPGs go, Kenshi’s versatility is nearly unmatched. It feels less like a game built around one genre and more like a game that keeps absorbing the best ideas from others.
+
+ Love isometric RPGs like Wasteland or Pillars of Eternity? Kenshi gives you the freedom, systems and party management you’d expect, but drops you into a world that refuses to revolve around your story. Prefer colony sims like RimWorld or Stranded: Alien Dawn? You’ll find similarly deep mechanics, except your colony exists within a much larger, more dangerous and politically complicated world. Enjoy the environmental storytelling of Elden Ring? Kenshi tells its story through ruins, scars, factions and the things you discover when you wander somewhere you were never meant to survive.
+
+ There’s a satisfying grind and progression system reminiscent of RuneScape, minus the shackles of an MMO. There’s a dynamic trade economy, faction politics, base-building, slavery, warfare, exploration and even faction creation. And if you want multiplayer, there’s apparently a mod for that, too.
+
+ You get the point: Kenshi is extraordinarily versatile. It can become the game you want it to be.
+
+ But that flexibility comes at a cost.
+
+ Kenshi does not hold your hand. Not even a little.
+
+ You’ll be confused. You’ll be directionless. You’ll get beaten half to death by starving bandits, enslaved, robbed, eaten or otherwise reminded that you are not the protagonist of this world. When you begin, you’re so weak and unequipped that even surviving can feel like an accomplishment. I wouldn’t blame anyone for falling off within the first hour.
+
+ That initial frustration is the barrier. It is also the point.
+
+ Because Kenshi isn’t interested in giving you a heroic journey. It gives you a starting condition: a nobody with no money, no power and no guarantee that tomorrow will be better than today. Your story only begins once you figure out how to survive long enough to write it.
+
+ Eventually, the confusion starts to give way to…</div></div><div class="citation"><div class="meta mono">▲ recommends · 3.1 hrs · 2026-07-07</div><div class="body">This game was interesting, good concept, good graphics and fantastic art-style, but man, the controls and difficulty is beyond a joke, in 2026, its not pleasant playing a game that plays like 2000s retro RPG, control wise, and the lack of tutorials is a joke. 
+
+ I recommend tho</div></div><div class="citation"><div class="meta mono">▲ recommends · 12.7 hrs · 2026-07-04</div><div class="body">Stumbled upon this a month ago, best purchase all year!
+ There is no guide no objective no main story.
+ join play learn repeat! This game is really what you make it into.
+ You stumble upon oh i didn&#x27;t know you could do that 1000 times a playthrough.
+ I&#x27;m only 12hrs in but I&#x27;m hooked!</div></div></details></div><div class="claim"><p class="text">Reviewers report a lack of in-game tutorials and note that the game does not guide or hold the player&#x27;s hand.</p><details><summary><span class="tag mono">▸ 2 reviews</span><span class="cta">Show receipts</span></summary><div class="citation"><div class="meta mono">▲ recommends · 3.1 hrs · 2026-07-07</div><div class="body">This game was interesting, good concept, good graphics and fantastic art-style, but man, the controls and difficulty is beyond a joke, in 2026, its not pleasant playing a game that plays like 2000s retro RPG, control wise, and the lack of tutorials is a joke. 
