  Some more explained details on the world, the in game mechanics and a more interactive tutorial wouldn&#x27;t go amiss. But besides these 2 things I don&#x27;t really have any complaints about it, except that I would personally like if the dialogue was voice acted. It does what it&#x27;s supposed to incredibly well, the mod support is amazing with many fun additions you can throw into the game quite easily.

  I was a bit sceptical at first since the gameplay looked more action oriented than it is, and the game doesn&#x27;t have controller support. But a good way to describe the controls is Kotor, but with less combat options, base building and a larger party system.

  Overall I give Kenshi 8.5/10. If guns (natively, not through mods), a longer and interactive tutorial, and voice acting are added it&#x27;ll easily become a full 10/10!</div></div><div class="citation"><div class="meta mono">▲ recommends · 66.6 hrs · 2026-05-26</div><div class="body">I always struggle to review games like this, because the community is amazing and consistently releases new content and mods for this game. With that, I&#x27;ll just be touching on the vanilla release, as with mods you can make it into whatever you want.
  
  So Kenshi, what is it? It&#x27;s a squad based open world game with a focus on community, allowing you to build your own structures, towns, and even empire. Unlike most other games of this nature, theres a huge focus on individual&#x27;s rather than hero units or trainable soldiers. Your main team will be your main team for a majority of your sessions. I found it quite difficult to manage more than 3 squads at a time, 2 exploration teams and a 3rd to run and guard the base. This works well and allows you to limit the size of your operation to whatever you personally find managable.
  
  Kenshi is a real time strategy, so you wont be influencing fights directly as much as youll be managing squad macro and keeping your people alive and healthy. The main hurdle when starting is learning that you&#x27;re MEANT to get your ass kicked a few times. It&#x27;s just counterintuitive and hard to learn. 
  
  I have nothing but nice things to say about this janky buggy mess, I adore it and if you put the time in you might as well. New players would probably benifet from a tutorial start, but I&#x27;m not sure Kenshi even cares if you play it. Its a desolate world that would keep on scrapping by, with or without you. The ancient robots, ruins and sparse wastes hold several worlds worth of lore and story just waiting to be found. The lore is probably the best part of Kenshi, realizing this world is much older and much more complicated than you ever imagined. Strong 8/10 from me.
  
